#X obj 10 970 cnv 1 1260 200 empty empty TRY\ THIS 8 12 0 13 #e6f6e9 #1d3557 0;
#X text 30 996 1) Raise the volume and drag x and y: the sound morphs between the presets \, the bars show the mix. Switch walk on and the cursor wanders by itself., f 56;
#X text 30 1047 2) Pick preset 5: the cursor jumps there \, yet the sound is not quite preset 5 - see the error at the presets. Press 10 rounds of the delta rule a few times and watch the error fall. Exact trains until it is gone., f 56;
#X text 446 996 3) Width 0.15: the pad breaks into tiles and the sound jumps from preset to preset - a codebook with no in-between. Width 1.5: everything washes into one average sound., f 56;
#X text 446 1062 4) Exact with width 1 or more: thousands of rounds \, a largest weight far above 1 \, and between the presets the parameters overshoot into their limits - exact interpolation with wide bumps is ill-conditioned., f 56;
#X text 862 996 5) Make your own preset: move the cursor to an empty spot \, dial the six sound sliders \, pick a preset number and press store. Move carries the picked preset (and its sound) to the cursor., f 56;
#X text 862 1062 6) Put two presets close together with very different sounds \, exact on: a steep cliff appears in the middle of a smooth pad \, and the weights swing hard., f 56;
#X connect 304 0 305 0;
#X connect 304 0 306 0;
